Here's the structured JSON object for the `multi_tool_use.parallel` function call as per your instructions:

```json
{
  "tool_uses": [
    {
      "recipient_name": "functions.extract_legal_clauses",
      "parameters": {
        "documents": [
          "https://www.company.com/contracts/agreement1.pdf",
          "https://www.company.com/contracts/terms_of_service.pdf",
          "https://www.company.com/contracts/privacy_policy.pdf"
        ],
        "clause_types": [
          "data_handling",
          "data_retention",
          "data_breach_notification"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "recipient_name": "functions.compare_clauses_to_regulations",
      "parameters": {
        "extracted_clauses": "output_of_extract_legal_clauses",
        "regulatory_requirements": "https://www.regulations.com/data_protection_standard.json"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

Please note that the actual extraction of clauses will depend on the response from the `extract_legal_clauses` function, which is not included here due to its dynamic nature based on the input parameters. Once the clauses are extracted, we can proceed with comparing them against the regulatory requirements using the `compare_clauses_to_regulations` function.<|im_end|>

